module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Adjunction.Additive
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleWire.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedSections.Braided
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafRankOne.Basic

/-!
# The section ring of an invertible sheaf of modules is commutative

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/GradedSections/Monoidal.lean` makes
`Γ_*(L) = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} (𝟙_ C ⟶ L ^⊗ n)` a graded ring in any monoidal category `C` with
`[Preadditive C]` and `[(MonoidalCategory.tensorRight L).Additive]`, and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/GradedSections/Braided.lean` makes it **commutative** under the extra hypothesis
`Stacks.GradedSections.HasTrivialSelfBraiding L`, namely `(β_ L L).hom = 𝟙 (L ⊗ L)`. Those files
are abstract: no geometric statement can use them until the three hypotheses are discharged for an invertible
sheaf of modules. This file discharges all three, and the last of them is the one with
mathematical content.

**The self-braiding.** For a general object of a symmetric monoidal category the hypothesis is
false — an invertible object may self-braid by `-1` — so something geometric must be used, and
what is used is local triviality. The argument has four steps, each a declaration below.

1. `braiding_eq_id_of_cyclic`: in `ModuleCat R` over a *commutative* ring, the transposition of
   `M ⊗[R] M` is the identity as soon as `M` is generated by one element: `m = r • e` and
   `n = s • e` give `n ⊗ₜ m = (s * r) • (e ⊗ₜ e) = (r * s) • (e ⊗ₜ e) = m ⊗ₜ n`. This is the
   whole of the commutativity of the ring of sections, and it is why the structure sheaf being
   a sheaf of *commutative* rings is indispensable.
2. `braiding_comp_toSheafify`: the braiding of a presheaf of modules is sectionwise that
   transposition (Mathlib's `PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.braiding_hom_app`), so for a presheaf whose
   sections are cyclic on a covering sieve of every object — the predicate `IsLocallyCyclic` —
   the braiding becomes the identity after the sheafification unit, by separatedness of a sheaf.
   The braiding itself is **not** the identity at the presheaf level: the sections of an
   invertible sheaf over a non-trivializing open need not be cyclic.
3. `sheafify_map_braiding`: hence sheafification sends it to the identity, by faithfulness of the
   unit correspondence of a left adjoint (`map_eq_of_unit_comp_eq`).
4. `braiding_eq_id_of_localization` plus `braiding_eq_id_of_iso`: the braiding on
   `SheafOfModules` is the localized one, so on an object of the form `P^#` it is the braiding of
   `P` conjugated by the monoidality isomorphism (Mathlib's `Localization.Monoidal.β_hom_app`);
   and every sheaf of modules is isomorphic to the sheafification of its own underlying presheaf.

The geometric input is then exactly clause 2 of Stacks Tag 0B8M in the form this repository
already proves it, `Stacks.SheafRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_isInvertible`: nothing
beyond local triviality is needed, and no new descent argument is written here.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.IsLocallyCyclic`: a presheaf of modules whose sections are
  generated by one element on a covering sieve of every object of the site.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.braiding_eq_id_of_isLocallyCyclic`: **a locally cyclic sheaf of
  modules has trivial self-braiding.**
* `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.hasTrivialSelfBraiding`: **an invertible sheaf of modules on a
  ringed space whose stalks are local rings has trivial self-braiding**, as an instance of the
  class the commutativity file asks for.
* `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.presheafMonoidalPreadditive`: presheaves of modules over a
  presheaf of commutative rings are monoidal preadditive. Absent from Mathlib, and the source of
  the additivity hypothesis at the sheaf level.
* `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.tensorRightAdditive`: **tensoring on the right in
  `SheafOfModules` is an additive functor**, which is the hypothesis
  `(MonoidalCategory.tensorRight L).Additive` of the graded-ring construction.
* `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.sectionCommRing`: **`Γ_*(L)` is a commutative ring** for an
  invertible sheaf of modules on a ringed space whose stalks are local rings, and
  `schemeSectionCommRing` is the same for a scheme, with no hypothesis.
* `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.natTensorPow_eq_tensorPow`: in nonnegative degree the abstract
  tensor power the graded ring is built from is the integer tensor power of Stacks Tag 01CU.
* `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.unitModuleSectionCommRing`: the fully concrete case,
  `Γ_*(X, 𝒪_X)` a commutative ring on an arbitrary scheme with no hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

**Local instances.** `Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory`, `braidedCategory` and
`sheafifyMonoidal` are deliberately `def`s, and the presheaf-level monoidal and symmetric
structures over `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf` are `local instance`s
there, so every section below whose statement mentions `⊗`, `𝟙_` or `β_` reintroduces them with a
local-instance attribute. This is what the sibling files do and it is unavoidable: nothing is
declared globally, because on a site with chosen finite products a global monoidal structure on
`SheafOfModules` would collide.

**Transparency.** Three identifications are definitional and used as such, never by rewriting.
`(Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj` and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureRingPresheaf 𝒪` are equal only at default
transparency, so the bridging monoidal-preadditive instance
`presheafMonoidalPreadditiveStructure` is stated in the second spelling and transported by
`change`, exactly as `Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules` is.
`CategoryTheory`'s `LocalizedMonoidal` is a type synonym for `SheafOfModules`, so Mathlib's
`Localization.Monoidal.β_hom_app` is *not* found by `rw` against a goal written in the
`SheafOfModules` spelling — `braiding_eq_id_of_localization` isolates that one rewrite in the
uniform `toMonoidalCategory` spelling and is applied by `exact`.
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.toSheafify` is by definition the unit of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.sheafifyAdjunction`, which is why
`map_eq_of_unit_comp_eq` applies to it with no bridging step; it too is applied by `exact`, since a
`rw` with `Adjunction.homEquiv_unit` fails on a goal mentioning `PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing`.

**Universes.** The whole braiding argument is polymorphic in the site universes `v u` and the
module universe `w` independently, as the monoidal structure on `SheafOfModules` is; no
`SmallCategory` hypothesis and no internal hom appear, so the universe constraint that
`Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalClosed` carries is not inherited. The ringed-space and scheme
sections are monomorphic in `u`, which is what `Stacks.SheafRankOne` and `Scheme` force.

**Why the additivity does not go through the internal hom.** `tensorLeft L` is a left adjoint
once `Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalClosed` is available, and a left adjoint between
preadditive categories is additive; but that route needs `[SmallCategory C]` and the structure
presheaf valued in `CommRingCat.{u}`. The route taken instead — transport the additivity of the
canonical tensor functor `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor` at `L` (the objectwise tensor
product is additive, `PresheafOfModules.tensorHom_add_right`, and so is sheafification) across
`Stacks.SheafInternalHom.tensorLeftIso` and then across Mathlib's `tensorLeftIsoTensorRight` —
needs neither, so the additivity holds at the same generality as the braiding, needing only weak
sheafification of abelian-group-valued presheaves, and `SheafOfModules` is preadditive with no
hypothesis at all — in particular the abelian structure of
`Mathlib/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/Abelian.lean`, which does need `HasSheafify`, is not
used.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)

## What is not done

No Stacks attribute is attached to anything here.

The carrier of the graded ring is still `𝟙_ C ⟶ L ^⊗ n` rather than the literal global sections
`Γ(L ^⊗ n, ⊤)` that the tagged statements use; the comparison is the sibling file
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SectionRingGeometric/GlobalSections.lean`.

Nothing is stated for negative exponents, so the graded module of Stacks Tag 01CV is still not
constructed, and `Stacks.GradedSections.powAdd` is still not shown to be an isomorphism.
`IsLocallyCyclic` is not shown to be equivalent to local freeness of rank one, only implied by it;
the converse would need the sections over a trivializing open to be recovered from cyclicity,
which is false without a covering hypothesis.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂ v u w

open CategoryTheory Category MonoidalCategory Limits Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification
  Opposite
open TopologicalSpace

namespace Stacks.SectionRingGeometric

/-! ### Cyclic modules transpose trivially -/

/-- In a tensor square, two scalar multiples of one element commute. -/
theorem tmul_comm_smul {R : Type u₁} [CommRing R] {M : Type u₂} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (r s : R) (e : M) : (s • e) ⊗ₜ[R] (r • e) = (r • e) ⊗ₜ[R] (s • e) := by
  rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul_smul, TensorProduct.smul_tmul_smul, mul_comm]

/-- **The braiding of a cyclic module with itself is the identity.** Over a commutative ring a
module generated by a single element `e` has `m ⊗ₜ n` and `n ⊗ₜ m` both equal to a scalar
multiple of `e ⊗ₜ e`, by the same scalar. This is the one place commutativity of the ring of
scalars is used, and the reason the section ring is commutative. -/
theorem braiding_eq_id_of_cyclic {R : Type u₁} [CommRing R] (M : ModuleCat.{u₁} R)
    (e : M) (he : ∀ m : M, ∃ r : R, m = r • e) : (β_ M M).hom = 𝟙 (M ⊗ M) := by
  refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (TensorProduct.ext' fun m n ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := he m
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := he n
  show (β_ M M).hom (m ⊗ₜ n) = m ⊗ₜ n
  rw [ModuleCat.MonoidalCategory.braiding_hom_apply, hr, hs, tmul_comm_smul]

/-! ### Two transport lemmas -/

/-- A trivial self-braiding transports along an isomorphism: `β_ A A` and `β_ B B` are conjugate
by the isomorphism tensored with itself, which is itself an isomorphism. -/
theorem braiding_eq_id_of_iso {D : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} D] [MonoidalCategory D]
    [BraidedCategory D] {A B : D} (e : A ≅ B) (h : (β_ B B).hom = 𝟙 (B ⊗ B)) :
    (β_ A A).hom = 𝟙 (A ⊗ A) := by
  have hn := BraidedCategory.braiding_naturality e.hom e.hom
  rw [h, comp_id] at hn
  have : IsIso (e.hom ⊗ₘ e.hom) := inferInstance
  exact (cancel_mono (e.hom ⊗ₘ e.hom)).mp (hn.symm.trans (id_comp _).symm)

/-- A left adjoint identifies two morphisms as soon as they agree after the unit of the
adjunction: the unit correspondence is a bijection. -/
theorem map_eq_of_unit_comp_eq {D : Type u₁} {E : Type u₂} [Category.{v₁} D] [Category.{v₂} E]
    [Preadditive D] [Preadditive E] {F : D ⥤ E} {G : E ⥤ D} (adj : F ⊣ G) {A B : D}
    (f g : A ⟶ B) (h : f ≫ adj.unit.app B = g ≫ adj.unit.app B) : F.map f = F.map g := by
  refine (adj.homEquiv A (F.obj B)).injective ?_
  rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit, Adjunction.homEquiv_unit, Adjunction.unit_naturality,
    Adjunction.unit_naturality, h]

/-- **A trivial self-braiding descends through a monoidal localization.** On an object in the
image of the localization functor the braiding is the braiding upstairs conjugated by the
monoidality isomorphism, so it is the identity as soon as the localization functor sends the
braiding upstairs to the identity. Stated in the `toMonoidalCategory` spelling, which is what
makes Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Localization.Monoidal.β_hom_app` applicable by `rw`; the
localized category is a type synonym, so a goal written downstairs matches only by `exact`. -/
theorem braiding_eq_id_of_localization {D : Type u₁} {E : Type u₂} [Category.{v₁} D]
    [Category.{v₂} E] (F : D ⥤ E) (W : MorphismProperty D) [MonoidalCategory D] [W.IsMonoidal]
    [F.IsLocalization W] [BraidedCategory D] {unit : E} (ε : F.obj (𝟙_ D) ≅ unit) (A : D)
    (h : (Localization.Monoidal.toMonoidalCategory F W ε).map (β_ A A).hom = 𝟙 _) :
    (β_ ((Localization.Monoidal.toMonoidalCategory F W ε).obj A)
      ((Localization.Monoidal.toMonoidalCategory F W ε).obj A)).hom = 𝟙 _ := by
  rw [Localization.Monoidal.β_hom_app F W ε A A, h, id_comp,
    Functor.Monoidal.μ_δ (Localization.Monoidal.toMonoidalCategory F W ε)]

/-! ### Locally cyclic presheaves of modules -/

section LocallyCyclic

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (𝒪 : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w})

/-- A presheaf of modules is **locally cyclic** when every object of the site carries a covering
sieve all of whose objects have cyclic modules of sections. A sheaf of modules that is finite
locally free of rank one is locally cyclic, which is the only way the predicate is produced
below; it is stated separately because that is all the braiding argument consumes. -/
def IsLocallyCyclic (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (P : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪) : Prop :=
  ∀ U : C, ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U ∧ ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (f : Y ⟶ U), S f →
    ∃ e : P.obj (op Y), ∀ m : P.obj (op Y), ∃ r : 𝒪.obj (op Y), m = r • e

section
attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules

/-- Over an object whose module of sections is cyclic, the self-braiding of a presheaf of modules
is the identity: the braiding of presheaves of modules is sectionwise the braiding of modules. -/
theorem braiding_app_eq_id (P : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    (e : P.obj U) (he : ∀ m : P.obj U, ∃ r : 𝒪.obj U, m = r • e) :
    (β_ P P).hom.app U = 𝟙 ((P ⊗ P).obj U) := by
  exact (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.braiding_hom_app P P U).trans
    (braiding_eq_id_of_cyclic (R := 𝒪.obj U) (P.obj U) e he)

end

end LocallyCyclic

/-! ### Sheafification kills the self-braiding -/

section Sheafify

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  (𝒪 : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w})
  (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules

/-- **The self-braiding of a locally cyclic presheaf of modules is the identity after the
sheafification unit.** The braiding is sectionwise a transposition of a tensor square, which is
the identity on a cyclic module; so the two composites agree on a covering sieve of every object,
and the target is a sheaf, hence separated. The braiding itself is in general *not* the identity
before sheafifying. -/
theorem braiding_comp_toSheafify (P : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪)
    (hP : IsLocallyCyclic 𝒪 J P) :
    (β_ P P).hom ≫ toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P) = toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P) := by
  refine PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun U ↦ ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun x ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hcyc⟩ := hP U.unop
  refine Stacks.SheafRankOne.isSeparated_val 𝒪 h𝒪 ((sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).obj (P ⊗ P))
    U.unop S hS _ _ fun Y f hf ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hcyc f hf
  have key : (P ⊗ P).map f.op ((β_ P P).hom.app U x) = (P ⊗ P).map f.op x := by
    rw [← PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (β_ P P).hom f.op x,
      braiding_app_eq_id 𝒪 P (op Y) e he]
    rfl
  have h1 := (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P)) f.op
    ((β_ P P).hom.app U x)).symm
  have h2 := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P)) f.op x
  exact h1.trans ((congrArg (fun z ↦ (toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P)).app (op Y) z) key).trans h2)

/-- **Sheafification sends the self-braiding of a locally cyclic presheaf of modules to the
identity.** -/
theorem sheafify_map_braiding (P : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪)
    (hP : IsLocallyCyclic 𝒪 J P) :
    (sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).map (β_ P P).hom = 𝟙 ((sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).obj (P ⊗ P)) :=
  (map_eq_of_unit_comp_eq (sheafifyAdjunction 𝒪 h𝒪) (β_ P P).hom (𝟙 (P ⊗ P))
      ((braiding_comp_toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 P hP).trans (id_comp _).symm)).trans
    ((sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).map_id _)

end Sheafify

/-! ### The self-braiding of a sheaf of modules -/

section SheafBraiding

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  (𝒪 : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w})
  (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory

/-- **A locally cyclic sheaf of modules has trivial self-braiding.** The braiding on
`SheafOfModules` is the localized braiding, so on the sheafification of a presheaf of modules it
is the braiding upstairs conjugated by the monoidality isomorphism; and a sheaf of modules is
isomorphic to the sheafification of its own underlying presheaf of modules. -/
theorem braiding_eq_id_of_isLocallyCyclic (L : SheafOfModules.{w} (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪))
    (hL : IsLocallyCyclic 𝒪 J L.val) : (β_ L L).hom = 𝟙 (L ⊗ L) :=
  braiding_eq_id_of_iso ((Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyCounitIso 𝒪 h𝒪).app L).symm
    (braiding_eq_id_of_localization (sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪) (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.localIso 𝒪 h𝒪)
      (Iso.refl _) L.val (sheafify_map_braiding 𝒪 h𝒪 L.val hL))

end SheafBraiding

/-! ### Additivity of the tensor functors -/

section Additive

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (𝒪 : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w})

/-- **Presheaves of modules over a presheaf of commutative rings are monoidal preadditive.**
Both the additive structure and the whiskerings are sectionwise, so this is Mathlib's
`MonoidalPreadditive (ModuleCat R)` applied object by object. Absent from Mathlib. -/
instance presheafMonoidalPreadditive :
    MonoidalPreadditive (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪) where
  whiskerLeft_zero := by intros; ext1 U; simp; rfl
  zero_whiskerRight := by intros; ext1 U; simp; rfl
  whiskerLeft_add := by intros; ext1 U; simp; rfl
  add_whiskerRight := by intros; ext1 U; simp; rfl

variable {J : GrothendieckTopology C} (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules

/-- `presheafMonoidalPreadditive` in the spelling the sheaf level uses, transported by hand for
the transparency reason recorded in the module docstring. -/
local instance presheafMonoidalPreadditiveStructure :
    MonoidalPreadditive (PresheafOfModules.{w} (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj) := by
  change MonoidalPreadditive (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪)
  infer_instance

/-- Sheafification of presheaves of modules is additive, being a left adjoint whose right
adjoint is additive. -/
local instance sheafifyAdditive : (sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).Additive :=
  (sheafifyAdjunction 𝒪 h𝒪).left_adjoint_additive

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory

/-- **Tensoring on the left in `SheafOfModules` is additive.** By
`Stacks.SheafInternalHom.tensorLeftIso` it is the canonical tensor functor
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor` at `L`, the sheafification of the objectwise tensor
product with `L`, and both the objectwise tensor product and sheafification are additive. -/
local instance tensorLeftAdditive (L : SheafOfModules.{w} (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪)) :
    (tensorLeft L).Additive := by
  refine @Functor.additive_of_iso _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ?_ _
    (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.tensorLeftIso 𝒪 h𝒪 L).symm
  refine ⟨fun {G G'} f g ↦ ?_⟩
  exact (congrArg (sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).map
    (PresheafOfModules.tensorHom_add_right (𝟙 L.val) f.val g.val)).trans
      ((sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).map_add)

/-- **Tensoring on the right in `SheafOfModules` is additive**, the two tensor functors being
isomorphic through the braiding. This is the hypothesis `(tensorRight L).Additive` that the
graded ring of sections is built under. -/
local instance tensorRightAdditive (L : SheafOfModules.{w} (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪)) :
    (tensorRight L).Additive :=
  Functor.additive_of_iso (BraidedCategory.tensorLeftIsoTensorRight L)

end Additive

/-! ### The geometric input: local triviality -/

section RingedSpace

open AlgebraicGeometry

variable {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}}

/-- A presheaf of modules sectionwise trivial on a family of opens covering the space is locally
cyclic: the covering sieve of an open `U` is the one whose objects lie inside some member of the
family, and over such an open the local basis element of the trivialization generates. -/
theorem isLocallyCyclic_of_cover_trivialization
    (P : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{u} X.presheaf) (V : X → Opens X) (hV : iSup V = ⊤)
    (t : ∀ x : X, Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization X.presheaf P (V x)) :
    IsLocallyCyclic X.presheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) P := by
  intro U
  refine ⟨⟨fun Y _ ↦ ∃ z, Y ≤ V z, ?_⟩, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro Y Z f ⟨z, hz⟩ g
    exact ⟨z, (leOfHom g).trans hz⟩
  · intro x hx
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.mp (hV ▸ Opens.mem_top x)
    exact ⟨V z ⊓ U, homOfLE inf_le_right, ⟨z, inf_le_left⟩, ⟨hz, hx⟩⟩
  · rintro Y f ⟨z, hz⟩
    refine ⟨((t z).comp (homOfLE hz)).basisAt (𝟙 Y), fun m ↦ ?_⟩
    exact ⟨_, ((t z).comp (homOfLE hz)).eq_smul_basisAt (𝟙 Y) m⟩

variable (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
    (structureRingPresheaf X.presheaf))

/-- **An invertible sheaf of modules on a ringed space whose stalks are local rings is locally
cyclic.** This is clause 2 of Stacks Tag 0B8M as
`Stacks.SheafRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_isInvertible` proves it, read through
`isLocallyCyclic_of_cover_trivialization`. -/
theorem isLocallyCyclic_val_of_isInvertible
    (L : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf X.presheaf h𝒪))
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf h𝒪 L]
    [∀ x : X, IsLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x)] :
    IsLocallyCyclic X.presheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) L.val := by
  obtain ⟨V, hV, ht⟩ :=
    Stacks.SheafRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_isInvertible h𝒪 L
  exact isLocallyCyclic_of_cover_trivialization L.val V hV fun x ↦ (ht x).some

/-! ### The section ring -/

section SectionRing

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory
  presheafMonoidalPreadditiveStructure sheafifyAdditive tensorLeftAdditive tensorRightAdditive

variable (L : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf X.presheaf h𝒪))
  [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf h𝒪 L]

/-- In nonnegative degree the abstract tensor power that the graded ring of sections is built
from is the integer tensor power of Stacks Tag 01CU. The hypothesis that `L` is invertible is
not needed for the left-hand side; it is needed for the right-hand side to exist at all, the
integer powers being defined through a chosen tensor inverse. -/
theorem natTensorPow_eq_tensorPow (n : ℕ) :
    Stacks.TensorPowers.natTensorPow L n =
      AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorPow X.presheaf h𝒪 L (n : ℤ) :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorPow_natCast X.presheaf h𝒪 L n).symm

variable [∀ x : X, IsLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x)]

/-- **An invertible sheaf of modules on a ringed space whose stalks are local rings has trivial
self-braiding.** This is the hypothesis that commutativity of the graded ring of sections needs,
and the one with mathematical content. -/
instance hasTrivialSelfBraiding : Stacks.GradedSections.HasTrivialSelfBraiding L :=
  ⟨braiding_eq_id_of_isLocallyCyclic X.presheaf h𝒪 L
    (isLocallyCyclic_val_of_isInvertible h𝒪 L)⟩

/-- **The graded ring of sections of an invertible sheaf of modules is commutative.** All four
hypotheses of `Stacks.GradedSections.instCommRing` are in place: the monoidal and braided
structures of `Stacks.SheafInternalHom`, preadditivity of `SheafOfModules` from Mathlib (an
unconditional instance, with the hom groups those of the underlying presheaves of modules),
additivity of `tensorRight` from `tensorRightAdditive`, and the trivial self-braiding from
`hasTrivialSelfBraiding`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def sectionCommRing : CommRing (Stacks.GradedSections.sectionRing L) :=
  inferInstance

end SectionRing

end RingedSpace

/-! ### Schemes -/

section Scheme

open AlgebraicGeometry

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory
  presheafMonoidalPreadditiveStructure sheafifyAdditive tensorLeftAdditive tensorRightAdditive

/-- The braided structure on the sheaves of modules over a scheme, in Mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling. The sibling file provides the monoidal and the
monoidal closed structures in that spelling but not the braided one, which is what a statement
about `β_` on `X.Modules` needs: instance search is keyed syntactically and does not unfold the
`def` `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def schemeBraidedCategory (X : Scheme.{u}) :
    letI := Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory X
    BraidedCategory X.Modules :=
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory X.presheaf
    (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X)

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory schemeBraidedCategory

/-- Preadditivity in the `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling. -/
noncomputable local instance schemePreadditive (X : Scheme.{u}) : Preadditive X.Modules :=
  inferInstanceAs (Preadditive (SheafOfModules.{u}
    (structureSheaf X.presheaf (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X))))

/-- Additivity of `tensorRight` in the `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling. -/
local instance schemeTensorRightAdditive (X : Scheme.{u}) (L : X.Modules) :
    (tensorRight L).Additive :=
  tensorRightAdditive X.presheaf (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X) L

variable (X : Scheme.{u}) (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- **An invertible module on a scheme has trivial self-braiding**, with no hypothesis: the
stalks of a scheme are local rings. -/
instance schemeHasTrivialSelfBraiding : Stacks.GradedSections.HasTrivialSelfBraiding L :=
  hasTrivialSelfBraiding (X := X.toRingedSpace)
    (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X) L

/-- **`Γ_*(X, L)` is a commutative ring**, for an invertible `𝒪_X`-module on a scheme, with no
hypothesis. This is the fact that Stacks Tag 01CV's graded ring is commutative. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def schemeSectionCommRing : CommRing (Stacks.GradedSections.sectionRing L) :=
  sectionCommRing (X := X.toRingedSpace)
    (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X) L

/-- **A fully concrete instance: `Γ_*(X, 𝒪_X)` is a commutative ring** on any scheme, with no
hypothesis at all. The structure sheaf is an invertible module over itself
(`Stacks.Ample.isInvertibleModule_unit`), so this is `schemeSectionCommRing` with every
side condition discharged. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def unitModuleSectionCommRing (Y : Scheme.{u}) :
    CommRing (Stacks.GradedSections.sectionRing (Stacks.Ample.unitModule Y)) :=
  schemeSectionCommRing Y (Stacks.Ample.unitModule Y)

end Scheme

end Stacks.SectionRingGeometric
